Outside, it is raining continuously.
I take my umbrella and walk to the nearby market.
I need some vegetables to make the curry.
I reach my usual vegetable shop.
I look at my list.
I ask the vendor for the vegetables.
"First, give me two large onions," I say.
"Then, three tomatoes too," I add.
He takes the onions and tomatoes.
"After that, I need some ginger and green chilies."
He puts all of it in a bag.
"Do you need anything else?" he asks.
"One small packet of coriander powder too," I say.
He adds the packet to the bag.
"How much is the total?" I ask.
"Sixty rupees," he says.
I give him the money.
Then, I take the vegetables.
Now, I must go to the butcher shop and buy the chicken.
I open my umbrella again and walk forward.
